<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baldwin V, Count of Hainaut</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1150–1195</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Baldwin VIII of Flanders, Baldwin the Courageous</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baldwin V was count of Hainaut from 1171 and, through his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-i-of-denmark">Margaret I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, count of Flanders as Baldwin VIII from 1191 until his death in 1195. He also secured Namur, raised into a margraviate for him by imperial grant. His daughter Isabella married Philip II Augustus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and his son Baldwin became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. His chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gislebert-of-mons">Gislebert of Mons</a> chronicled his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-v-count-of-hainaut.jpg" alt="Baldwin V, Count of Hainaut" width="294" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olivier De Wree,Lambertus Vossius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baldwin8.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
